---
import CodeBlock from "@/components/code-block.astro";
import Docs from "@/layouts/docs.astro";
import { docHref } from "@/lib/docs";
import { OBSERVABLE_DOCS, repoTree } from "@/lib/site";

const install = `pnpm add @statewalker/vcs-commands @statewalker/vcs-core @statewalker/vcs-working-tree`;

const minimal = `import { Git } from "@statewalker/vcs-commands";
import { createMemoryHistory } from "@statewalker/vcs-core";
import {
  createMemoryCheckout,
  createMemoryGitStaging,
  createMemoryWorkingCopy,
  createMemoryWorktree,
} from "@statewalker/vcs-working-tree";

const history = createMemoryHistory();
await history.initialize();
await history.refs.setSymbolic("HEAD", "refs/heads/main");

const staging = createMemoryGitStaging();
const checkout = createMemoryCheckout({ staging });
const worktree = createMemoryWorktree({ blobs: history.blobs, trees: history.trees });
const git = Git.fromWorkingCopy(createMemoryWorkingCopy({ history, checkout, worktree }));

await worktree.writeContent("README.md", new TextEncoder().encode("# Hello\\n"));
await git.add().addFilepattern(".").call();
const commit = await git.commit().setMessage("Initial commit").call();
console.log(commit.id);`;

const onDisk = `import { Git } from "@statewalker/vcs-commands";
import { createGitFilesBackend, openGitLinkedWorktrees } from "@statewalker/vcs-store-files";
import { createNodeFilesApi } from "@statewalker/vcs-utils-node/files";

// An existing repository (or create: true for git init): native git and this code share it.
const files = createNodeFilesApi({ rootDir: "/path/to/repo" });
const { history } = await createGitFilesBackend({ files, gitDir: ".git" });
const worktrees = await openGitLinkedWorktrees({ files, gitDir: ".git", history });
const git = Git.fromWorkingCopy(await worktrees.openCurrent());

for await (const c of await git.log().setMaxCount(5).call()) {
  console.log(c.id.slice(0, 7), c.message.split("\\n")[0]);
}`;

const clone = `import { createMemoryHistoryWithOperations } from "@statewalker/vcs-core";
import { createRepositoryFacade, createTransportRefStore, fetch, lsRemote } from "@statewalker/vcs-transport";

const history = createMemoryHistoryWithOperations();
await history.initialize();

const refs = await lsRemote("https://example.com/some/repo.git"); // Map<ref name, id>

// Smart HTTP, protocol v2 when the server speaks it (in a browser the server must allow CORS).
const result = await fetch({
  url: "https://example.com/some/repo.git",
  repository: createRepositoryFacade({ history }),
  refStore: createTransportRefStore(history.refs),
  refspecs: ["+refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/*"],
});
for (const u of result.refUpdates) console.log(u.summary, u.localRef); // [new branch] refs/remotes/origin/main`;

const fromSources = `corepack enable          # Node.js 24, pnpm 10.16.1 (pinned in packageManager)
pnpm install
pnpm build               # packages' exports point at dist/: build before running apps
pnpm test
pnpm --filter @statewalker/vcs-example-01-quick-start start`;
---

<Docs title="Getting started" description="Install StateWalker VCS, write a first commit with the porcelain API, open a repository on disk, and fetch over HTTP.">
  <h1>Getting started</h1>
  <p>
    StateWalker VCS is a set of npm packages. You compose a repository from three parts, a
    <strong>history</strong> (objects and refs), a <strong>checkout</strong> (index, HEAD,
    operation state) and a <strong>worktree</strong> (the files), and drive it with the
    <code>Git</code> facade, whose commands mirror git's and JGit's. Every package is ESM with
    type declarations and runs in browsers, Node.js and workers.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={install} lang="sh" title="terminal" />
  <p>
    Add a storage backend when the repository must outlive the process:
    <code>@statewalker/vcs-store-files</code> (a real <code>.git</code> directory over a
    <code>FilesApi</code>), <code>vcs-store-sql</code>, <code>vcs-store-kv</code> (IndexedDB and
    similar), and <code>@statewalker/vcs-transport</code> to fetch and push.
  </p>

  <h2>A first commit</h2>
  <p>The minimal program, in memory. It is also the <a href="/examples/quick-start">first live example</a>: run it in this tab.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={minimal} lang="ts" title="first-commit.ts" />
  <p>
    Commands are objects: configure them with chainable setters, then <code>call()</code> once.
    <code>git.add()</code>, <code>commit()</code>, <code>status()</code>, <code>log()</code>,
    <code>branchCreate()</code>, <code>checkout()</code>, <code>merge()</code>,
    <code>rebase()</code>, <code>stash*()</code>, <code>fetch()</code>, <code>push()</code>,
    <code>clone()</code> and more are listed in the
    <a href={docHref("packages/vcs-commands/README.md")}>vcs-commands reference</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>A repository git can open</h2>
  <p>
    <code>@statewalker/vcs-store-files</code> reads and writes git's own layout: loose objects,
    packs and their indexes, loose and packed refs, reflogs, the binary index. A repository written
    here is one <code>git log</code>, <code>git status</code> and <code>git fsck</code> accept, and
    the reverse. In a browser, pass any other <code>FilesApi</code> (memory, OPFS); the
    <a href="/examples/git-directory">.git directory example</a> builds one in a tab and lets you
    download it.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={onDisk} lang="ts" title="open-on-disk.ts" />

  <h2>Fetch and push</h2>
  <p>
    <code>@statewalker/vcs-transport</code> speaks git's wire protocol (v1 and v2) over smart HTTP
    or any duplex byte stream: a <code>MessagePort</code>, a WebRTC data channel, a webrun-streams
    channel. The <a href="/examples/fetch-push">fetch &amp; push example</a> runs both directions
    between two repositories in a tab.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={clone} lang="ts" title="fetch.ts" />

  <h2>From the sources</h2>
  <p>
    The repository is a pnpm workspace: packages under <code>packages/</code>, eleven numbered
    Node tutorials under <a href={repoTree("apps/examples")}><code>apps/examples</code></a>,
    demos under <a href={repoTree("apps/demos")}><code>apps/demos</code></a>, benchmarks under
    <code>apps/benchmarks</code>, and this site under <code>site/</code>.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={fromSources} lang="sh" title="terminal" />
  <p>
    The package references on this site are the packages' own <code>README.md</code> files, rendered
    as they are in the repository. The <a href={OBSERVABLE_DOCS}>Observable page</a> on GitHub Pages,
    built from <code>docs/</code> with Observable Framework, is a one-page summary of the same
    project: its features and the quick start above.
  </p>

